      "summary": "global/country-language-mismatch — PWA Component",
      "description": "As a Developer, \nI want a reusable global/country-language-mismatch React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \nso that it can be consumed across storefronts to surface country and language mismatch prompts to shoppers in a consistent drawer pattern.\nThe component covers two variants, both rendered as a right-anchored drawer panel using the shared drawer shell:\nLocation Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's IP-detected country does not match the current storefront (consumed by \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-823\n )\nLanguage Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's browser language does not match the current EU storefront locale (consumed by \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-689\n)\nThe component does not own the trigger logic or redirect behaviour — that is handled by the consuming stories. It exposes callbacks for each CTA action and accepts props to control which variant renders.",
